Necromancer Epic Quest	25	{"kind":"quest","title":"Necromancer Epic Quest","wikiPath":"/Necromancer_Epic_Quest","sources":[{"kind":"quest","where":"Nektulos Forest","detail":"Start zone"},{"kind":"quest","where":"Venenzi Oberzendi","detail":"Quest giver"}],"components":[{"name":"Flowing Black Robe","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Flowing_Black_Robe"},{"name":"Manisi Herb","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Manisi_Herb"},{"name":"Cloak of Spiroc Feathers","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Cloak_of_Spiroc_Feathers"},{"name":"Slime Blood of Cazic Thule","qty":1,"wikiPath":"/Slime_Blood_of_Cazic_Thule"}],"rewards":[{"text":"Twisted Bone Earring","item":"Twisted Bone Earring","wikiPath":"/Twisted_Bone_Earring"},{"text":"Apprentice Ring","item":"Apprentice Ring","wikiPath":"/Apprentice_Ring"},{"text":"Scythe of the Shadowed Soul","item":"Scythe of the Shadowed Soul","wikiPath":"/Scythe_of_the_Shadowed_Soul"}],"card":{"title":"Necromancer Epic Quest","lines":["Recommended Level: 46+","Classes: Necromancer","Related Zones: Various","Related NPCs: Various"]},"links":["Nektulos Forest","Necromancer","Twisted Bone Earring","Apprentice Ring","Scythe of the Shadowed Soul","Torment of Shadows","Venenzi Oberzendi","Kazen Fecae","Sir Edwin Motte","Najena (NPC)","Flowing Black Robe","Rolling Stone Moss","Emkel Kabae","Ssessthrass","Swamp of No Hope","Scaled Symbol of the Serpent","Grand Herbalist Mak`ha","Royal Sarnak Herbalist","Chardok","Manisi Herb","A bone golem","A failed apprentice","A tortured soul","Drendico Metalbones","Timorous Deep","Jzil GSix","An azarack","Silver Disc","A gorgalask","Spiroc Feathers","Keeper of Souls","Black Silk Cape","Cloak of Spiroc Feathers","Innoruuk (God)","Eye of Innoruuk","Cazic Thule (God)","Slime Blood of Cazic Thule","Gkzzallk","Gkzzallk in a Box","Lake Rathetear","Chill Sight","Plane of Hate","Lord of Ire","Lord of Loathing","Master of Spite","Fright","Dread","Terror","Plane of Fear","Tome of Instruction","Najena","Plane of Sky"],"dialogue":[{"npc":"Kazen Fecae","text":"Excellent!' You watch Kazen hold the head by the hair and begin to cast a spell. A flash of darkness centers around the head and the eyes of the dead knight open, a terrible scream emanating from its lips. 'This poor fool here - I think I will keep him in my bag from now on. You have done well, my new apprentice. Take this symbol and know that you can do other tasks to advance within my apprentice ranks."},{"npc":"Venenzi Oberzendi","text":"What is it you want! Can't you see I am gathering reagents for my [master]? If I don't get them for him quickly he might punish me."},{"npc":"Venenzi Oberzendi","text":"You do not know of my teacher? The great Kazen Fe'cae! I am one of his illustrious apprentices! If you fancy yourself a necromancer, travel to Lake Rathetear and tell Kazen you wish to study the dark arts."},{"npc":"Venenzi Oberzendi","text":"My master is working on some great project. He's always busy studying an old text he found and murmuring something about following in the footsteps of Miragul."},{"npc":"Kazen Fecae 's eyes seem to glow as he turns to you and","text":"Leave me be if you have no reason to be here, mortal!"},{"npc":"Kazen Fecae","text":"The wandering 'knight' Sir Edwin Motte recently slew one of my lesser servants. This foolish knave travels from town to town pretending to be 'good.' Separate his head from his body and return it to me so I may work my magics upon it. This fool will become another plaything for me, even in death."},{"npc":"Kazen Fecae","text":"Excellent!' You watch Kazen hold the head by the hair and begin to cast a spell. A flash of darkness centers around the head and the eyes of the dead knight open, a terrible scream emanating from its lips. 'This poor fool here - I think I will keep him in my bag from now on. You have done well, my new apprentice. Take this symbol and know that you can do other tasks to advance within my apprentice ranks."},{"npc":"Kazen Fecae","text":"I share great secrets with my more powerful servants who show me they are willing to serve without question. Tell my servant the name of any symbol he gives you and he will instruct you. If I give you a symbol, speak its name to me so I may instruct you."},{"npc":"Kazen Fecae","text":"You have a long way to go before I teach you the true secrets of life and death. Visit Venenzi Oberendi in the Nektulos forest and show her the symbol. She is collecting reagents for one of my experiments and is taking far too long. I do not wish her dead, yet. I simply need the reagents soon. Retrieve the reagents and give them to my assistant Emkel Kabae. I do not wish to handle them myself."},{"npc":"Venenzi Oberzendi","text":"I see you serve my master as well now. I assume you are here to take the reagents from me which I have gathered for him? I don't know if I like the idea of you gaining the credit for my hard work here. I might consider giving you these reagents, if only you do a small [task] for me."},{"npc":"Venenzi Oberzendi","text":"Thank you. I did not think you would track down Najena and slay her. I think that I am going to return to my old life in Neriak. I am sick of the way Kazen has been treating me. He never seems to teach me anything worthwhile. Don't forget to give his lapdog that symbol with the reagents. I'm sure he will give you a new one."},{"npc":"Emkel Kabae","text":"I am Emkel Kabae, first apprentice to Kazen. If you have a symbol, tell me its name."},{"npc":"Emkel Kabae","text":"There are more reagents to be gathered. The time draws near for our master's ascension. Travel to the lands of Kunark and seek out Ssessthrass. He is a very wise Iksar herbalist helping me in my endeavor to please Master Kazen. Be careful not to insult his speech, or you may end up dead before you serve your purpose to the master. Be sure to show him the symbol as proof or he may consider you dinner."},{"npc":"Ssessthrass","text":"I do not wisssh to be bothered."},{"npc":"Ssessthrass","text":"Sssso, Emkel ssssent you to retrieve the manisi herb? I do not have the herb. The ssssarnak guard the herb. Apparently it is ssssacred to them. Only memberssss of their royal family are allowed to partake of it. They live deep in Chardok. They are hoarding what little of the precious herb there is. If you have an army, perhapssss you can bring me the herb and I can prepare it for Emkel. Bring back this ssssymbol as well."},{"npc":"Emkel Kabae","text":"You are truly worthy of studying with our master. Bear this new symbol and contemplate what you wish from life before you let go of it. Ask the master about the symbol of testing and he will explain all. I too was tested by him.' Emkel pulls up his sleeve to show a grievous scar from his wrist to his shoulder."},{"npc":"Emkel Kabae","text":"You must ask the master about the symbol of testing. Do not hand the symbol to him for he may interpret that as a breach of conduct."},{"npc":"Kazen Fecae","text":"Show me that you can overcome larger obstacles and manipulate servants. Gather a force for of mercenaries if you like, or so-called friends, if you desire, and prepare for battle, my promising young student. Return to me with the symbol of testing when you are prepared for battle with my creations. Have no fear, I will not slay you myself. If you do live, tell me the name of the symbol you receive."},{"npc":"Kazen Fecae","text":"As you hand Kazen the symbol, you hear him speak directly into your mind. 'Good luck, my student!' Kazen finishes an incantation and suddenly hands begin to reach up from the ground, as if they were pulling themselves from the grave all around you. A piercing scream fills the air as the creatures advance upon you!"},{"npc":"a bone golem","text":"Grrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrrraaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!"},{"npc":"Drendico Metalbones","text":"The hills ears keep spinning the wonders of wells. Twisting twisting fly in water scar hot horses. Teach me! Bring floating water islands of doom!"},{"npc":"Drendico Metalbones","text":"Seek, search, turn, twist! Kazen hopes to death master truly! Read out, read in between! Talk to the pretty clouds.' Drendico turns his back to you and throws a book over his shoulder. 'Bring back book! Bring back reagents three!!' He shouts as he mumbles some more gibberish."},{"npc":"Jzil GSix","text":"The test of power it is. Prove yourself worthy of power and bring me a silver disc, spiroc feathers, and a black silk cape. Only then will you know true power."},{"npc":"Jzil GSix","text":"This feathered cloak should be more than enough payment, now be gone from my sight!"},{"npc":"a thunder spirit princess","text":"Greetings, travelers, welcome to the Plane of Sky! We are thunder spirits - this first island is our home. You are welcome to stay here as long as you like. If you wish to go to other islands you may purchase keys from the Key Master."},{"npc":"a thunder spirit princess","text":"Gkzzallk lives far above here. We often take him tea because he's so nice to us fairies! He likes to chat with the others who live here and can often be found in the temple up above. If you give me a bit of money, I can go make sure he is home."},{"npc":"a thunder spirit princess","text":"Thank you, _____. I will tell him to expect visitors."},{"npc":"Gkzzallk","text":"Hello Stranger, would you care for some tea?"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T07:15:17.672Z","outOfEra":true}
